Description: fast native WhatsApp desktop client
 ZapFast is a lightweight WhatsApp client for the desktop, written in Rust
 with egui. It links to the WhatsApp account on your phone by QR code, like
 WhatsApp Web, and covers chats, media, voice and video calls, polls,
 notifications and a tray icon, opening in under a second. It is an
 unofficial client, not affiliated with WhatsApp or Meta.
 .
 The command is zapfast. It runs on X11 and Wayland. The message archive is
 encrypted with a key kept in the session's Secret Service keyring (GNOME
 Keyring, KWallet, KeePassXC), which every mainstream desktop provides.
 zenity is recommended as the file-dialog fallback when no desktop portal is
 running. Updates come through apt; the built-in updater stays off.
